    "abstract": "Illustrated parts breakdown of the cabin ceiling and wall wash lighting channel, showing the extrusion attachment hardware, the cabin and lobby partition lengths and the reading light interface items around them.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the cabin ceiling and wall wash lighting channel and the adjacent trim. Use it to order channel hardware, partitions and reading light interface items.",
      "figure_note": "The figure shows a typical cabin section looking aft, and the arrangement repeats along the deck. Items 30 and 40 are fitted only on aircraft that have not been converted to solid state strips; they are shown for identification and are no longer supplied. Items 22 and 62 are the lobby lengths of the two partitions and are keyed to zones 265 and 282. They are not alternates of items 20 and 60 and must not be substituted for them: the diffuser is cut to the same length as the partition it sits behind, so a cabin length fitted in the lobby leaves the run short by the width of one bay and the error is only found when the strips are clipped in. The cabin lengths at items 20 and 60 are marked as not applicable in the lobby for the same reason. The strip and the extrusion are supplied as a kit against the applicable service bulletin and are not catalogue items in this figure."
    },
